# DO NOT copy this to mobile-app/.env.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE is read at BUNDLE time (src/api.ts), so whatever a
# mobile-app/.env holds is baked into the next APK/IPA. A local address left in
# it ships to real phones, which then cannot reach the backend - and nothing in
# the build says so.
#
# Where the value belongs instead:
#   Builds (APK / IPA): eas.json's build profiles, already set to the hosted API.
#   A one-off local run: the shell, for that one command only:
#     EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8000 node node_modules/expo/bin/cli start --web --clear
#
# Values by target, for that shell variable:
#   Web preview on the same machine:  http://127.0.0.1:8000
#   Android emulator:                 http://10.0.2.2:8000
#   Physical device on your network:  http://<your-machine-LAN-IP>:8000
#   Hosted:                           https://poc.runiksoft.com  (the current host)
#
# Left commented out on purpose: copying this file anyway creates nothing that
# could be baked into a build.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=
